the department of medical informatics  and clinical epidemiology is a  department in the School of Medicine at  OHSU our research programs and  educational programs are synergistic in  that what the researchers look at is  reflected in the education the primary  focus of what we do is on information  and how we can use that information to  improve individual health healthcare  biomedical research and public health  informatics plays a crucial role in our  research the information that is  available about these patients and their  needs is enormous it's way too much  information for people to look through  and so we provide a way to summarize  that and prioritize that information my  research has to do with automated text  processing and automated text mining  what that means is automatically  extracting out knowledge from the  incredible volume of clinical and  publication tax that we have my  co-investigators and I use neural  imaging techniques to map functional  networks in the brain and specifically  we use techniques such as functional  magnetic resonance imaging and optical  micro angiography to measure changes in  blood flow and blood volume in the brain  this is very information-rich and we  have to use a lot of computational  approaches and integrate those  approaches ultimately with clinical  information to address the scientific  question apparent because the different  faculty use many different methods in  their research it really creates a  diverse array of techniques and research  subjects that benefit each other's  research and also our students  Oh Hsu is by its nature very  interdisciplinary we have such a broad  array of faculty and so many  opportunities to collaborate that people  of very different backgrounds can find a  home here it's not only being in  beautiful downtown Portland but it's  also the fact that our program is so  well balanced so that we're we're very  broad we cover most areas of informatics  we wind up with quite a range of people  at different stages of their informatics  career adventure that I think is a  really nice mix people choose OHSU over  other informatics educational  institutions because of the experience  of the faculty and because of the  opportunities here for learning  exploring and for projects we've got  students coming in at all levels  graduate students postdoctoral fellows  physicians who have completed residency  training and they come from both  mathematical sciences computational  sciences and the biological sciences I  actually got my education at OHSU the  education at OHSU is broadly based and  allows students to select their own  interests it's also one of the 17  national library medicine fellowship  programs and so when people come to OHSU  either on campus or through distance  learning they know that they're getting  their education from an institution that  is experienced in teaching informatics  professionals the distance learning  program has been really important to us  it's enabled individuals who want to  pursue careers and informatics to do so  without leaving their jobs or their  geographic location and so forth we  communicate with them by email we see  them at scientific meetings  conferences sometimes they combine visit  us so we get to know them well I've had  a great opportunity to mentor students  both in the distance learning program  and here on campus it's been wonderful  to see the opportunities that they've  taken and how they've launched their  careers usually starting from work that  they did here in the program we've  really done a fantastic job of reaching  lots of different learners and I think  that the department has a great  opportunity to really be at the center  both at the institution and really  nationally of providing pragmatic  solutions to the issues that plague not  only informatics itself but also the  broader healthcare system we have the  opportunity to use these tools to  improve the care of patients to make  that care and that experience better and  to make it more economical so this is a  really exciting time to be working in  the field of clinical informatics  because of the large volume and the  innovation in the research that we do we  push the field forward we look at new  ways to use information technology new  algorithms to apply to the data and so  forth and that benefits the field as a  whole
 

